{"content":"When multiple capabilities depend on the same well-structured representation of content, improving that representation can unblock them together. The meeting links fixing import and establishing “a robust read model” to long-term full-text search, HTML export, and a possible MCP endpoint.

This leverage holds when the downstream capabilities can consume the same read model; it does not imply that each capability needs no separate implementation. The team described import fixing as the higher priority and framed the read model as a foundation, not as a finished search or export feature.

A reader can predict that a weak or unreliable read model will delay several consumer features at once, while repairing it can reduce duplicated data-access work across those features.","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T15:38:34.370Z"}

